From d9f6d2443ca1cd4c9aefe7a882a1cb7f371e3f2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 19:31:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3 Plan B: hand-rolled SPI master against
 cycloneive_asmiblock primitive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces wb_altasmi_parallel.v body — was a thin Wishbone wrapper around
the altasmi_parallel megafunction (epcs_ctrl.v), now a hand-rolled SPI
master FSM driving cycloneive_asmiblock directly (5-port single-bit SPI
primitive, cycloneive_atoms.v line 7017).

Rationale: NH15+NH16-fw+NH17 wrapper iterations on the megafunction-
based path validated three useful primitives (byte-0 dummy lock; per-
byte event from read_add_reg edge; ctrl_reset stretcher) but each fix
traded one pipeline race for another (latch-overwrite → level-lock
re-latch → stage_cntr=2'b10 gating race).  Megafunction's
read_data_reg / dvalid_reg / read_add_reg have different clock edges +
gating conditions designed for an internal HardCopy config controller,
NOT external MMIO sampling.  Wrapper-layer patch budget exhausted in
Quartus 21.1 Lite Cyclone IV E.

Plan B scope (first round): READ path only (fast_read 0x0B opcode).
Write/erase paths stubbed (illegal_* tied to 0); CTRL bits b1/b2/b3/b4/
b5/b7 are MMIO-compatible no-ops.  CTRL.b6 reset + b8 fast_read level
keep their semantics so firmware Phase E (mode_epcs_probe one-byte-per-
op) does not need to change.

FSM: IDLE → PRE (4-cycle CS-to-SCK setup) → SHIFT (8 bits, MSB first,
SPI mode 0) → LOAD (1-cycle byte reload) → ... → PAUSE (CS held low,
wait firmware drain via STATUS.b1 + DATAOUT read) → TAIL (4-cycle CS
hold high) → IDLE.  Phase enum: CMD(0x0B) → A2 → A1 → A0 → DUM → DAT → ...
SCK = sysclk/4 = 12.5 MHz (EPCS16 fast_read supports >=25 MHz; 2x margin).
NH15 1-deep dataout slot preserved with byte_valid (per-byte 1-cycle
pulse) replacing the megafunction's level-locked am_data_valid.

Synthesis: 0 errors, 0 Critical Warnings (was 4x 169123 with altasmi).
LE 8682/10320 = 84%, -259 LE vs NH17 (8941).  Wrapper itself 215 LE.
ASMI blocks 1/1 (100%) placed on H1/D2/C1/H2 dedicated AS pins.
Setup slack -1.160 ns (was -1.182 ns NH17 — unchanged).  20 Warnings
are unused stub regs (ctrl_write etc. tied to GND) — expected.

Bitstream md5 16ee77945254dd5ec81cc23d5b3dac37 (368011 B).
Stage2 ELF unchanged (Phase E firmware compatible without changes).
