 rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v | 551 ++++++++++++++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 318 insertions(+), 233 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v b/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v
index 3de35ef..1542dfd 100644
--- a/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v
+++ b/rtl/wb_altasmi_parallel.v
@@ -1,50 +1,58 @@
-// wb_altasmi_parallel.v — thin Wishbone (NEORV32 XBUS) wrapper around the
-// Altera altasmi_parallel megafunction.  Drives the dedicated AS pins
-// (DCLK / nCSO / ASDO / DATA0) via USE_ASMIBLOCK=ON — no QSF pin
-// assignments needed.
+// wb_altasmi_parallel.v — Plan B hand-rolled SPI master against the
+// cycloneive_asmiblock primitive.  Preserves the MMIO interface
+// previously exposed over the altasmi_parallel megafunction wrapper,
+// so firmware (mode_epcs_probe Phase E one-byte-per-op) does not
+// need to change.
 //
-// Base: 0xF2000000.  1 MB decode window (xbus_adr[31:20] == 12'hF20).
+// Why: the altasmi_parallel megafunction has internal pipeline timing
+// races (read_data_reg / dvalid_reg / read_add_reg gated by different
+// stage_cntr conditions) that make external MMIO sampling unreliable.
+// NH15+NH16-fw+NH17 wrapper iterations validated three useful
+// primitives (byte-0 dummy lock; per-byte event from read_add_reg
+// edge; ctrl_reset stretcher) but each fix traded one race for
+// another — wrapper-layer patch budget exhausted in Quartus 21.1 Lite.
+//
+// Plan B: skip the megafunction.  Directly instantiate
+// cycloneive_asmiblock (5-port primitive: dclkin / scein / oe / sdoin
+// / data0out — Quartus 21.1 Lite Cyclone IV E, cycloneive_atoms.v
+// line 7017) and roll our own SPI master.  altasmi's own
+// instantiation at epcs_ctrl.v line 422 (sd3) confirms this primitive
+// is silicon-validated for AS-pin access (NH15 byte-0=0xff dummy
+// proved data round-trips through the pins).
+//
+// First-round scope: READ path only (fast_read 0x0B opcode), with the
+// existing NH15 1-deep dataout slot for firmware back-pressure.
+// Write/erase paths are stubbed (illegal_* flags wired to 0) and will
+// be added in a later round once the read path is silicon-validated.
 //
-// "Thin" model: MMIO exposes altasmi's raw control inputs and outputs;
-// firmware (Phase 3 epcs.c) drives the per-byte handshake.  Bits in CTRL
-// are split into LEVEL (read/write/sec_erase/rd_status — held until
-// firmware clears) and PULSE (shift_bytes/wren/reset — auto-clear after
-// one cycle).
+// Base: 0xF2000000.  1 MB decode window (xbus_adr[31:20] == 12'hF20).
 //
-// Register map (byte offsets, 32-bit accesses):
-//   0x00  CTRL    (W)  b0=reserved (NH9: removed — port_fast_read=PORT_USED
-//                                    causes qmegawiz 21.1 Lite to strip the
-//                                    `read` input port from the megafunction
-//                                    as a fast_read/read mutex.  Use b8.)
-//                      b1=write   (level)
-//                      b2=sector_erase (level)
-//                      b3=read_status  (level)
-//                      b4=shift_bytes  (1-cycle pulse)
-//                      b5=wren         (1-cycle pulse)
-//                      b6=reset        (1-cycle pulse; clears sticky flags)
-//                      b7=rden_drop    (1-cycle pulse; drops rden to 0 for
-//                                        one cycle to fire end_read_reg —
-//                                        firmware pulses after last byte
-//                                        of a read to terminate operation)
-//                      b8=fast_read    (level — opcode 0x0B + 24-bit addr +
-//                                        1 dummy byte; uses the stage3
-//                                        do_wait_dummyclk FSM-unlock that
-//                                        plain READ lacks — see comment at
-//                                        epcs_ctrl.v line 383 OR-term)
-//                  (R)  reads back the 4 level bits in matching positions
-//   0x04  ADDR    (R/W) [23:0]   altasmi.addr
-//   0x08  DATAIN  (R/W) [7:0]    altasmi.datain
-//   0x0C  STATUS  (R)   b0=busy
-//                       b1=data_valid_sticky (clears on DATAOUT read or reset)
-//                       b2=illegal_erase_sticky (clears on reset)
-//                       b3=illegal_write_sticky (clears on reset)
-//   0x10  DATAOUT (R)   [7:0]    latched altasmi.dataout (reading clears DV)
-//   0x14  ESTAT   (R)   [7:0]    altasmi.status_out (latest read_status result)
-//   0x18  RADDR   (R)   [23:0]   altasmi.read_address (live read-address
-//                                counter; primary purpose: prevent
-//                                synthesis pruning of read_add_cntr →
-//                                end_read_reg; secondary purpose: runtime
-//                                diagnostic of READ progress)
+// Register map (unchanged from the megafunction wrapper):
+//   0x00  CTRL    (W)  b1=write (level — IGNORED first round)
+//                      b2=sector_erase (level — IGNORED first round)
+//                      b3=read_status  (level — IGNORED first round; returns 0)
+//                      b4=shift_bytes  (1-cycle pulse — IGNORED; reads
+//                                        are now SCK-paced internally)
+//                      b5=wren         (1-cycle pulse — IGNORED first round)
+//                      b6=reset        (1-cycle pulse — aborts current op,
+//                                        clears sticky flags + dataout slot)
+//                      b7=rden_drop    (1-cycle pulse — IGNORED; CTRL=0
+//                                        is now the canonical termination)
+//                      b8=fast_read    (level — starts a FAST_READ op;
+//                                        clearing it terminates the op
+//                                        per NH10 auto-terminate semantics)
+//                  (R)  reads back the level bits in matching positions
+//   0x04  ADDR    (R/W) [23:0]   24-bit byte address for FAST_READ
+//   0x08  DATAIN  (R/W) [7:0]    write-data scratch (IGNORED first round)
+//   0x0C  STATUS  (R)   b0=busy   (any FSM state != IDLE)
+//                       b1=data_valid_sticky (latched_dataout has a fresh byte)
+//                       b2=illegal_erase_sticky (tied to 0 first round)
+//                       b3=illegal_write_sticky (tied to 0 first round)
+//   0x10  DATAOUT (R)   [7:0]    latched SPI receive byte (reading clears DV)
+//   0x14  ESTAT   (R)   [7:0]    tied to 0 (no RDSR path first round)
+//   0x18  RADDR   (R)   [23:0]   internal byte-progress counter for diagnostics:
+//                                  starts at ADDR on op entry, increments by 1
+//                                  per data byte successfully shifted in.
 
